## Vendored modules

`scripts/clawbio/` is a vendored subset of the upstream `clawbio` package:

- `__init__.py` — replaced by a **minimal** module exposing only `__version__ = "0.7.1"`.
  Upstream's `__init__.py` also does `from .runner import list_skills, run_skill,
  upload_profile`, which pulls in the full ClawBio skill runner (plugin/runner
  machinery). That runner is intentionally **not** vendored and not used here.
- `common/__init__.py` — unmodified; its PEP 562 lazy exports are safe because
  only the vendored submodules are ever imported.
- `common/parsers.py` — unmodified; stdlib-only at import time (`numpy` is
  imported lazily inside `parse_vcf_matrix`, which this skill does not call).
- `common/checksums.py` — unmodified; stdlib only.
- `common/report.py` — unmodified; imports `common.audit` and `common.checksums`.
- `common/audit.py` — unmodified; `opentelemetry` imports are `TYPE_CHECKING`
  or inside functions, so runtime needs only the stdlib. This skill does not
  write the audit log (the CLI never calls `write_audit_log`).
- `common/html_report.py` — unmodified; imports `report.DISCLAIMER`.
- `common/rec_shortener.py` — **added beyond the original vendor list** because
  the current `pharmgx_reporter.py` lazily imports it in
  `extract_phenotype_recs()` when ClinPGx enrichment is available. It is
  stdlib-only (`re`, `html.parser`). Without it that optional path would raise
  ImportError; the default offline CLI path does not touch it.

Vendored modules depend on the Python standard library only. The skill was
verified offline with Python 3.11+.

